From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Piotr Oniszczuk <piotr.oniszczuk@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 17:25:43 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] media: amvdec: s7: do not swap the AV1 RPM block

The S7 AV1 microcode is of the S4 generation and writes the RPM
parameter block in natural order. With the T7 word swap the RPM check
reports wrong values for every frame, e.g.:

  av1: firmware parsed type 0 hint 7 size 1920x1920, controls 1 32 1920x1080

Drop av1_rpm_swap from the S7 platform data, keep the host parser setup.

Signed-off-by: Piotr Oniszczuk <piotr.oniszczuk@gmail.com>
---
 .../media/platform/amlogic/amvdec/amvdec_platform.c   | 11 ++++++-----
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/amlogic/amvdec/amvdec_platform.c b/drivers/media/platform/amlogic/amvdec/amvdec_platform.c
index 4cd4912..d4cb3c8 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/amlogic/amvdec/amvdec_platform.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/amlogic/amvdec/amvdec_platform.c
@@ -664,10 +664,12 @@ const struct amvdec_platform meson_amvdec_platform_s6 = {
 };
 
 /*
- * S7: the S4 decoder with the DOS-bus canvas and the T7/S6 AV1 handling.
- * DMC port parking as on S6 but with its own status word (0xcc) and only
- * the HEVC front-end port (bit 7). The DOS register layout is the S4 one
- * for everything the driver touches.
+ * S7: the S4 decoder with the DOS-bus canvas and the AV1 host parser
+ * setup of T7/S6. The S7 microcode is of the S4 generation and stores the
+ * AV1 RPM block in natural order (no word swap). DMC port parking as on
+ * S6 but with its own status word (0xcc) and only the HEVC front-end port
+ * (bit 7). The DOS register layout is the S4 one for everything the
+ * driver touches.
  */
 const struct amvdec_platform meson_amvdec_platform_s7 = {
 	.formats = amvdec_formats_s4,
@@ -678,7 +680,6 @@ const struct amvdec_platform meson_amvdec_platform_s7 = {
 	.dmc_hevc_mask = BIT(7),
 	.dos_canvas = true,
 	.av1_host_parser = true,
-	.av1_rpm_swap = true,
 };
 
 MODULE_FIRMWARE("amrisc/amrisc_vc1.bin");
-- 
